%% Runtime attestation, slice B: watching (runtime-attestation.md, "Slice B: watching, report only"). Built, 2026-11-03: it reports, and nothing acts.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Op as Someone with access, or a fault
    participant API as Kubernetes API
    participant Att as Attestation agent
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant CA as Credentials agent

    Att->>API: watching every pod of Polar's namespaces, and what owns them
    alt a container dies by a signal
        Op->>API: the kubelet sets its state: exit 139, say
        API-->>Att: the pod's status. Seconds later a restart of the pod has overwritten it
        Att->>Att: a crash is a fact: reported at once, even while it doubts itself
    else a pod is changed, or made by hand
        Op->>API: kubectl debug, an image patched, a pod with no owner
        API-->>Att: the pod
        Att->>Att: held to its owner, each minute. A new pod can come before its owner, so it has to stand at two checks running
    end
    Att->>Att: an ERROR, once
    Att-)Bk: attestation-reports, and again each minute while it stands
    Bk-)CA: stamped with who published it
    CA->>CA: only from the attestation agent: logged, and one AttestationReported in the ledger, however often it is sent
    Note over CA: nothing follows. Refusing at renewal stays as it was, and shutting it down sooner is someone's choice: a signed revocation
